# Per-Dockerfile ignore (BuildKit) — paths relative to the build context root
# (the workspace dir holding kai-cli/ kai-core/ kai-engine/ kai-tui/). The
# Dockerfile COPYs only those four module dirs, so just prune heavy siblings +
# non-source weight from the context upload. (No `*` whitelist — it can strip
# the local module contents and make the replace/workspace build fetch the
# pinned tag.)
#
# kai-tui is NOT excluded: `kit`, the coding harness a Cloud Agent job runs, is
# built from it. Excluding it made the build fail with a bare
# "/kai-tui: not found" on the COPY, which reads as a missing directory rather
# than an ignored one.
kai-server/
old-kai/
bench/
**/.git
**/node_modules
**/testdata
